{
  "summary": "Updates the Guix time-machine commit to pick up upstream Guix package updates and bumps python-lief to 0.17.6 in CI lint requirements. In manifest_gui.scm, it also wraps python-lief and nsis-x86_64 to disable test execution on transitive dependencies (python-psutil, python-pytest-xprocess, python-sh) that fail when compiled natively on RISC-V architectures.",
  "problem": "Running Guix builds on native riscv64-linux hosts fails because python-lief 0.17.5 transitively depends on python-msgspec, which lacked riscv64 support in the older Guix pin. In addition, several transitive dependencies fail their test suites when built natively on riscv64.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description quotes the error on RISC-V systems: 'guix shell: error: package python-lief@0.17.5 does not support riscv64-linux', tracked in issue #36232.",
    "Upstream Guix issue 10128 documents native riscv64 test failures in packages like python-psutil."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
